            {
                "entry_id": "db3d258d-672a-3a7f-9cc5-39f31171a7a0",
                "word": "marchant",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0e0eef3b-8f75-4b88-a0c3-df7d91dc1f39",
                        "entry_id": "db3d258d-672a-3a7f-9cc5-39f31171a7a0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "marchants"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                        "entry_id": "db3d258d-672a-3a7f-9cc5-39f31171a7a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete form of merchant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ee38dc7-05e8-4956-98b8-bec3b6f7e17a",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "To whom they shewed, how those marchants were\nArriv'd in place their bondslaves for to buy […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5707403-0a8f-4617-917a-af66296c5af0",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "His wife (having invented a present shift) laughed on her husband, saying: What marchant I pray you have you brought home hither, to fetch away my tub for five pence, for which I poore woman that sit all day alone in my house have beene proffered so often seaven: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b63e648-e29c-4ab3-8b6f-f9aaf242722b",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "By Jove, master marchant, by sea or by land\nWould get but smale argent if I did not stand\nHis very good master, I may say to you,\nWhen he hazards in hope what hap will insue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a85e9bda-3018-405d-b91a-70b798e11fe4",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "Now by the chaunge of a vizard one man might play the king and the carter, the old nurse and the yong damsell, the marchant and the souldier or any other part he listed very conveniently."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96d26182-2d2a-4a92-b086-b4d80d68054e",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "Faith Gentlemen now I play a marchants part,\nAnd venture madly on a deſperate Mart."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c42ff596-a77e-4056-bfb5-cb20df12a8bf",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "‘What thinke you of this English, tel me I pray you.’ ‘It is a language that wyl do you good in England but passe Dover, it is woorth nothing.’ ‘Is it not used then in other countreyes?’ ‘No sir, with whom wyl you that they speake?’ ‘With English marchants.’ ‘English marchantes, when they are out of England, it liketh hem not, and they doo not speake it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e18a0b5-08d8-4473-bc2e-de6517ae144b",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "In an other corner, Mistris Minx, a marchants wife, that will eate no cherries, forsooth, but when they are at twentie shillings a pound, that lookes as simperingly as if she were besmeard, and iets it as gingerly as if she were dancing the canaries, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdb9be23-dfad-4318-b1b1-4b3697d30943",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "The Marchant that returnes from ſome far forrain lands,\nEſcaping dreadfull rocks and dangerous ſhelfs and ſands,\nWhen as he ſees his ſhip her home-hauen enter ſafe,\nWill he repine at God, and as offended chafe\nFor being brought to ſoone home to his natiue ſoile,\nFree from all perills ſad that threaten ſaylor’s ſpoile?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc91e188-1f85-4c03-8793-ea18c83cf804",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "The grasse and herbe doth fat sheepe in very short space, proued by English marchants which haue caried sheepe thither for fresh victuall and had them raised exceeding fat in lesse then three weekes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1ab7713-c3c8-4048-9148-b1102bee5e3a",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "You Marchant Mercers, and Monopolites,\nGain-greedy Chap-men, periur'd Hypocrites,\nDiſſembling Broakers, made of all deceipts,\nVVho falſifie your Meaures and your VVeights,\nT' enrich you ſelues, and your vnthrifty Sons\nTo Gentillize with proud poſſeſſions: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92ca01d4-e3a3-42a1-ab07-3ebeb1fcf08d",
                                "sense_id": "adb6bbaa-8183-3c08-ab13-a3ab5e3a0bb6",
                                "text": "\"An' he bes free times as old as herself,\" he wailed, \" an' ugly as a squid ! But he bes rich — rich as any marchant — an' for the bread an' the fixin's an' the gold she bes takin' 'im.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
